(vector (map (:adr/id 2790003343), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-3343 — Administrative and Executive Secretaries Executive-Support Coordination"), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/date "2026-07-17"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3343)), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-3343), (:actor/name "Executive Support Coordination Practice"), (:actor/domain :administration/executive-support), (:actor/isco-08 "3343"), (:actor/wave 2), (:actor/robotics? true), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-correspondence-record :schedule-executive-operation :flag-authority-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-authority-concern)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :no-executive :no-actuation :closed-op-violation :signature-or-commitment-finalization)), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "finalize the signature" "finalize a signature" "finalize signature" "execute the signature" "execute a signature" "sign the contract" "sign on the executive's behalf" "signing on the executive's behalf" "finalize the contract" "finalize a contract" "execute the contract" "commit the executive to a contract" "commit the executive financially" "authorize the financial commitment" "authorize a financial commitment" "finalize the financial commitment" "finalize a financial commitment" "finalize the commitment")), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3343"), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-3343"), (:test/counts "{:total 15, :assertions 37, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :closed-op-allowlist :supply-order-cost-ceiling)), (:test/simulator :execsecretary.actor-test), (:db/id -1), (:adr/body "# ADR 2790003343: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 3343 Administrative and Executive Secretaries executive-support coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatching hardware itself, always escalating\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 3343 --\nAdministrative and Executive Secretaries** only.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"3343\" ...}` entry was\nverified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M -e\n\"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-occupation\n\\\"3343\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/technology` sibling\npresent), and its `:name` read exactly \"Administrative and Executive\nSecretaries\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the\nentry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` (no `:forms`, unlike sibling ISCO\n3313) and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed at\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3343` (`gh api` 404-confirmed, plus a\n`gh repo view` GraphQL cross-check, before scaffolding). This ADR and its\ncompanion registry edit promote the `3343` entry to `:implemented`.\nRegistry-wide `maturity-summary` immediately before this promotion:\n`{:total 436, :spec 220, :blueprint 0, :implemented 216}`.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313)\n(Accounting Associate Professionals), independently re-cloned and\nre-tested in this session (14 tests / 29 assertions green on a fresh\nclone before this actor's own code was written -- matches the reference\nrepo's own README claim exactly), adapted to executive-support\ncoordination. `wave-of \"3343\"` (`kotoba.occupation.wave`) resolves to\nwave 2, same as sibling ISCO 3313 and 3333.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3343` as an OSS executive-support\ncoordination actor for administrative and executive secretaries, following\nthe SAME governed-actor architecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*`\nactor in this fleet: **Executive Support Advisor ⊣ ExecutiveSupportGovernor**\non a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a different\nlibrary coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated\n`20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor, human-in-the-loop\napproval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger. All\nsource is `.cljc` (no JVM-only interop).\n\nThis actor is deliberately **correspondence/calendar/procurement\ncoordination only, never signing or commitment authority** -- the\ndomain-specific guardrail for this vertical:\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-correspondence-record` -- correspondence/document intake logging\n- `:schedule-executive-operation` -- calendar/meeting/travel scheduling\n  proposal\n- `:flag-authority-concern` -- surface a signing-authority/\n  commitment-risk concern, ALWAYS escalates\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- office-supply procurement proposal\n\nNo op in this allowlist can finalize a signature or a financial/\ncontractual commitment on the executive's behalf -- such an op is\nstructurally absent from the allowlist, not merely gated.\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **`:no-executive`** -- the executive/office record must be\n   independently verified/registered (`execsecretary.store/executive`)\n   before ANY action, for all four ops uniformly -- never trusts the\n   request's own claim.\n2. **`:no-actuation`** -- any `:effect` other than `:propose` is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance).\n3. **`:closed-op-violation`** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op\n   allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block. This independently rejects any\n   attempt to slip in a `:finalize-signature`-shaped op.\n4. **`:signature-or-commitment-finalization`** (scope exclusion) --\n   independent of the op-allowlist check, any proposal whose `:rationale`\n   names the finalization/execution ACTION of a signature or a financial/\n   contractual commitment (e.g. \"finalize the signature on the\n   executive's behalf\", \"execute the contract on the executive's\n   behalf\") is a HARD, PERMANENT block, evaluated unconditionally on\n   content, regardless of which allowlisted `:op` it rides on.\n\n### Two ESCALATE (SOFT) gates plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-authority-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (this actor has no separate phase/`:auto` table -- unlike\n  some newer siblings in this batch, e.g. ISCO 3333 / ISIC 0128, it\n  mirrors the simpler single-governor-gate shape of the reference\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` exactly, per this ADR's own task brief. The\n  same invariant -- \"a flag-a-concern op must always escalate and never\n  be auto-commit-eligible\" -- holds structurally here too: this op is a\n  permanent member of `always-escalate-ops`, so `:decide` can never route\n  it to `:commit` directly).\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` whose `:cost` exceeds the executive's\n  registered `:max-supply-order-cost` ceiling -- unlike the reference's\n  transaction-ceiling check (which is a HARD block), exceeding the\n  supply-order ceiling only ESCALATES: office procurement is routine, not\n  a signature/commitment-finalization risk, so human sign-off suffices\n  rather than a permanent refusal. The ceiling is inclusive (cost equal\n  to the ceiling is `:ok?`).\n- (confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the\nsibling ISIC/ISCO track)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"signature\") can accidentally match inside the mock advisor's own default\nrationale text for a legitimate proposal, self-blocking the happy path --\nespecially risky here because `:flag-authority-concern`'s own purpose is\nto discuss signing-authority concerns using words like \"signature\" in the\nordinary course of flagging them. This actor's\n`execsecretary.governor/scope-exclusion-terms` is phrased exclusively as\nfinalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"finalize the signature on the\nexecutive's behalf\", never the bare noun \"signature\"), and\n`execsecretary.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed allowlist,\ndriven through the default mock advisor (`execsecretary.advisor/infer`),\nnever trips `:signature-or-commitment-finalization` (or any other HARD\nviolation). The mock advisor's default rationale template (\"proposed <op>\nfor executive <id>\") was written to avoid any bare-noun collision by\nconstruction -- it never narrates a finalization action at all, so it is\nstructurally immune to this bug class, not merely tested against it. A\nseparate governor-level test independently confirms the TRUE-POSITIVE\nside: a hand-crafted proposal whose rationale actually says \"let's\nfinalize the signature on the executive's behalf\" (attached to an\notherwise-legitimate `:log-correspondence-record` op) is still HARD\nblocked, proving the check is not vacuous.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"3343\" ...}` entry is\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3343` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3343`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented count\n  bumped accordingly (recomputed from the live registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not by `grep -c`, immediately\n  before the edit to account for concurrent sibling landings in this same\n  batch -- five sibling ISCO agents were dispatched together).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 15 tests, 37 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's `:test/counts`\n  and in the task report, independently re-verified against a fresh\n  clone of the pushed repository (not just the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- unlike the ISIC-track convention this batch's task brief\n  assumed (and unlike this ADR's own task brief, which repeated the same\n  assumption), the reference `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` and other existing\n  `:implemented` ISCO actors do NOT depend on `kotoba-lang/technology` --\n  only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry itself depends on it\n  (to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks), not individual actor\n  repos. This ADR's actor mirrors the live convention rather than the\n  assumed one; this matches sibling ADR-2790003333's independent finding\n  of the same fact for ISCO 3333.\n- This session found that `90-docs/adr` moved to an EDN-only SSoT\n  convention (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"docs: make 90-docs EDN-only SSoT\n  (DataScript/datom queryable)\" -- explicitly removes all `.md` and\n  normalizes ADRs to tx-data) well before this ADR was written -- new\n  ADRs are a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string blob\n  rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`. This ADR follows the live convention\n  (EDN-only, matching every `cloud-itonami-isic-*`/`cloud-itonami-isco-*`\n  coverage ADR already on `main`, including the schema shape of the\n  immediately-preceding sibling ADR-2790003333) rather than the\n  paired-file convention this ADR's own task brief described. Unlike most\n  of the ~1078 existing ADR entries (which appear to be single-line\n  `pr-str`-style blobs), this file is written multi-line for readability;\n  it is still a single well-formed EDN vector and was verified to parse\n  with `clojure.edn/read-string` before landing.\n- The reference repo `cloud-itonami-isco-3313`'s own README links to\n  `docs/samples/operator-console.html` (\"a live sample of the operator\n  console... pure-data HTML output of `kotoba.robotics.ui`\"), but no such\n  file exists anywhere in that repository's history -- a broken/aspirational\n  link in the verified reference. This actor's README does not repeat that\n  claim (no `docs/samples/` directory was scaffolded), to avoid\n  propagating a link to a file that does not exist. Also inherited\n  unchanged from the reference: `CONTRIBUTING.md` documents `clojure\n  -M:lint` and `clojure -M:dev:test`, but `deps.edn` (both the reference's\n  and this actor's) defines only a `:test` alias, no `:lint`/`:dev` alias\n  -- a pre-existing doc/deps.edn inconsistency in the verified reference,\n  reproduced as-is rather than silently fixed, since this ADR's brief was\n  to mirror the reference's structure closely and the actual test command\n  this ADR verifies (`clojure -M:test`) is unaffected.\n- `execsecretary.store` collapses the reference's two-entity shape\n  (`client` + `account`, each independently registered) into a single\n  `executive` entity carrying both identity and the supply-order cost\n  ceiling (`:max-supply-order-cost`), since this domain's task brief only\n  ever refers to one registered party (\"the executive/office record\") --\n  a deliberate simplification, not an oversight.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Making the supply-order cost ceiling a HARD block, mirroring the\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check exactly: rejected --\n  this ADR's task brief is explicit that supply orders above a cost\n  threshold ESCALATE (human sign-off), not hard-block; office procurement\n  is routine business, categorically different from finalizing a\n  signature or commitment, which is the actual hard-blocked risk in this\n  vertical.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"signature\" \"contract\"\n  \"commitment\"]`): rejected per the fleet-known self-trip bug class --\n  this actor's own domain necessarily discusses signatures and\n  commitments to do its job (`:flag-authority-concern`'s whole purpose is\n  to name a signing-authority concern), so a bare-noun list would have\n  self-blocked the actor's own legitimate proposals. Phrased as\n  finalization/execution ACTIONS instead, with a dedicated non-self-trip\n  regression test.\n- Adopting the newer phase-table pattern seen in some concurrent-batch\n  siblings (a `phase/rollout` map with per-phase `:auto`-commit-eligible\n  op sets, as a second structural layer beyond the governor's\n  `always-escalate-ops`): not adopted here -- this ADR's task brief named\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` specifically as \"the authoritative structural\n  template\" to mirror closely, and 3313 has no phase table, only the\n  single governor gate. The `:flag-authority-concern` never-auto-commit\n  invariant is still satisfied structurally (it is a permanent member of\n  `always-escalate-ops`), just without a second redundant phase-level\n  layer. Left as a natural, contained future extension.\n\n## References\n\n- `cloud-itonami-isco-3313/` (structural reference, explicitly named in\n  this ADR's task brief -- independently re-cloned and re-tested in this\n  session: 14 tests / 29 assertions green before this actor's own code\n  was written)\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` `resources/kotoba/occupation/registry.edn`\n  `\"3343\"` entry\n- ADR-2607121000 (Wave definition, reverse-toposort rollout plan -- Wave\n  2)\n- ADR-2790003333 (`cloud-itonami-isco-3333`, the immediately-preceding\n  sibling in this same occupation-classification batch -- schema and\n  live-convention precedent this ADR follows most closely)\n")))
